    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d428">

                <pb facs="0645" n="557" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg557"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hirsch to Mr. Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-04-12"><hi rendition="#italic">April 12, 1892</hi></date>.
                        (Received April 25.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 427.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The missionaries of the American
                    Presbyterian Church have been established for many years among the Nestorians of
                    Urumiah, in Persia. During all of that time they have had teachers and book
                    agents among the Nestorians, across the frontier line, in the district of
                    Garvar, in Turkey.</p>
                <p>I have just been informed of the closing, two years ago, of six of those schools
                    and of the arrest last month of five of the teachers.</p>
                <p>In order to bring the matter to the attention of the Government, I have to-day
                    addressed a note to the Sublime Porte, of which a copy is inclosed herewith.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Solomon Hirsch.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d428-a1.xml" xpointer="d428-a1"/>
            </div>
